How to Reproduce
Open Packet Tracer and build the topology in docs/01-requirements-and-design.md using the cabling in docs/02-addressing-and-port-map.md.
Paste configs/switch-config.txt into the switch CLI, then configs/router-config.txt into the router CLI.
Configure end devices and the wireless client using configs/end-devices.md.
Run the checks in docs/04-verification-and-testing.md.

Replace every <CHANGE_ME> placeholder with your own credentials. Never commit real passwords from production devices.

Results
Test	Expected	Result
Office PC to gateway, printer, POS (inter-VLAN)	Success	Pass
POS terminal to gateway and receipt printer	Success	Pass
Guest laptop to its own gateway	Success	Pass
Guest laptop to Office VLAN	Blocked	Pass
Guest laptop to POS VLAN	Blocked	Pass

Full steps are in docs/04-verification-and-testing.md.

Known Limitations
The ISP-facing interface has no IP address, so there is no NAT, default route or real internet access yet. This is the next lab.
The access point is placed in the guest VLAN for lab simplicity. Production designs usually manage the AP from a separate management VLAN.

See docs/06-limitations-and-next-steps.md.

